EXPERIMENT 1: Lists, Links and Images
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Fruits and Vegetables</title>

<script>
function show(n,i,d)
{
    document.getElementById("info").innerHTML =
    "<h2>"+n+"</h2><img src='"+i+"' width='200'><p>"+d+"</p>";
}
</script>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Fruits and Vegetables</h1>
<h3>25K65A1203</h3>
<h2>Fruits</h2>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Apple',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Red_Apple.jpg',
'Apple is rich in Vitamin C')">Apple</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Banana',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8a/Banana-Single.jpg',
'Banana is rich in potassium')">Banana</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Mango',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Hapus_Mango.jpg',
'Mango is rich in vitamins')">Mango</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Orange',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/Orange-Fruit-Pieces.jpg',
'Orange is rich in Vitamin C')">Orange</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Grapes',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bb/Table_grapes_on_white.jpg',
'Grapes contain antioxidants')">Grapes</a>
<h2>Vegetables</h2>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Carrot',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Carrots_of_many_colors.jpg',
'Carrot is rich in Vitamin A')">Carrot</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Potato',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/Patates.jpg',
'Potato gives energy')">Potato</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Tomato',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/88/Bright_red_tomato_and_cross_section02.jpg',
'Tomato is rich in Vitamin C')">Tomato</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Spinach',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/34/Spinach_leaves.jpg',
'Spinach is rich in iron')">Spinach</a><br>
<a href="#" onclick="show('Brinjal',
'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7b/Aubergine.jpg',
'Brinjal is rich in fiber')">Brinjal</a>
<div id="info">
<h3>Click a name to see image and information</h3>
</div>
</body>
</html>
